load ../pinned-progressions.maude

--- Coverage: the progression completes -- region steps, clean exit, post
--- steps, terminal.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* workflowDone(f1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage (THE pinning claim): the admission trigger is consumed mid-flight
--- and the progression STILL completes -- bindings are values, matching gates
--- only admission.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* trig(f1, consumed) workflowDone(f1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: the lapse arm is reachable -- a break before the region drains
--- routes to lapsed with the arm's commit stamped.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* region(f1, lapsed) lapseAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage (point of no return): a post-region step commits AFTER the break
--- in log order -- statements outside the region consult no condition.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* condBroken(M:Cnt) postAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that lt(M:Cnt, N:Cnt) .

--- Coverage (repair): the condition breaks and REPAIRS before any advancing
--- commit observed the broken window -- the progression completes with no
--- lapse. `workflowDone` requires `region(_, done)`, and lapsed never becomes
--- done, so this state PROVES no lapse occurred despite `brokeEver`.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* brokeEver workflowDone(f1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage (re-admission, Decision 4): two DISTINCT firings -- fact identity
--- is admission identity -- each complete independently.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init2 =>* workflowDone(f1) workflowDone(f2) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (fate-at-commit): no region step ever commits while the
--- condition stands broken -- the stateful break stamp coexisting with a
--- LATER step stamp is unreachable (the check is atomic with the commit).
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* condBroken(M:Cnt) stepAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that lt(M:Cnt, N:Cnt) .

--- Invariant (lapse exactly once per firing): two lapse commits of the SAME
--- firing are unreachable -- its region cell is consumed into lapsed.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* lapseAt(f1, M:Cnt) lapseAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (no silent stall): no FINAL state strands an open region --
--- every progression ends done, lapsed, or terminal. The reactive bite below
--- proves this non-vacuous.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>! region(f1, open(K:Cnt)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (lapse is terminal for the region): a lapsed firing never reads
--- as done -- the two exits are exclusive by construction.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* lapseAt(f1, N:Cnt) region(f1, done) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (the region gates its point of no return): a post-region step
--- never commits while the region is still open -- [apply] requires done, and
--- done is only reached by draining every step under the condition.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* region(f1, open(K:Cnt)) postAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (today's semantics stall silently): under reactive re-derivation --
--- continuations require the trigger to still match and the guard to still
--- hold, no lapse rule -- a FINAL state with the region still open is
--- reachable: the silent stall observed live in manual ch. 15.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-REACTIVE-PROGRESSION :
  init =>! region(f1, open(K:Cnt)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .
